---
description: A review finding is about the pull request head it was written on; a review the owner asks for is posted on the pull request
alwaysApply: true
---

# Review findings

A comment on a pull request is about that pull request's head. Read it against that head before calling the pull request ready to merge.

A finding that asks for a change is still open when that head does not contain the change. Say so. A later pull request stacked above the head does not resolve it.

A finding that is tried and not adopted is answered with the measurement or the reason, on the pull request it was written on (`.cursor/rules/bench.mdc`).

Before acting on a finding or declining it, check its claim against the code of that head: run the reproduction, or read the lines it names. A finding can be right about the reader's difficulty and wrong about the fact.

A fix a finding proposes (a formula, a bound, a count) is derived again before it goes into the design or the code. PR #146's finding proposed ⌈|Δθ| √(r / 2ε)⌉ pieces for a polar segment; the term 2|Δr||Δθ| of a segment whose radius and angle both change was missing, and one piece of a segment with Δθ = 0.1 and Δr = 540 would have been 0.89 pixels off where 0.25 was the bound.

A finding that asks to change a decision the owner made is not declined by citing the rule that records the decision. Reply with what the decision was and what the finding shows, and ask the owner (`.cursor/rules/consent.mdc`).

A review the owner asks for is posted on the pull request, in the same turn, without waiting for an ask to post it. A review shown only in the conversation is not seen by anyone else, and the pull request does not show that it was reviewed. A re-review after fixes is posted the same way.

Before calling a PR ready, before reporting that a PR waits for review, and whenever the owner asks for the next step, read the reviews and inline comments of every open PR (`gh pr view <n> --json reviews,comments` and `gh api repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/<n>/comments`). PR #146's report said that its checks had passed and that it waited for review; a review with two findings was already on it, and the owner had to point to it.

A reply that says a finding was fixed is checked against the pushed diff first (`git show <sha>` holds the change). In PR #100 an edit of `PlotPlan.Render`'s XML was lost to a later edit, and the reply said it was done. In PR #219 a reply said that a test of a binned area's `Baseline` was added; the pushed commit had the check without the test, and the re-review found it. Each "added" or "fixed" in a reply names what in the diff holds it.

Read the pull request's comments again just before posting a reply to a review: a re-review can land while the reply waits for the checks, and a reply posted without reading it answers a review that is no longer the latest.

```text
# BAD
The chunk-boundary check is missing. A later pull request sits on this head, so merge.

# GOOD
The chunk-boundary check is not in this head. The finding stays open.
```

```text
# BAD
Owner: 12をレビューして下さい
Agent: writes the findings in the conversation, and asks whether to post them

# GOOD
Owner: 12をレビューして下さい
Agent: posts the findings as a comment on the pull request, and gives the link and a summary in the conversation
```
